<h3>4. If the Window Closes</h3>
<ul>
<li>Automated penalty assessment issues on the discrepancy and full period (£1,204.15 + surcharge on £30,360.32)</li>
<li>Registration flagged to marketplaces under joint-liability reporting — selling permissions may be withheld</li>
<li>Reinstatement requires agent intervention with original records (recovery timelines of 8–12 weeks)</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#FFF8E1;padding:12px">HMRC knows that "submit your records through
this link" is the classic phishing shape — your suspicion is the correct default. Three checks: the filing
reference above matches the one in your agent's copy of the deferral letter; the submission page displays
your registration number and period before any upload field; and records go only to this reference-bound
page, never to an email address. The window date, however, is set by the deferral schedule, not by our
convenience.</p>

